{
  "ranking": [
    {
      "id": "patch_c67689a4876b",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 250,
      "mechanism": "The first observed mismatch is cycle 8 where input_axis_tready is 0 but expected 1. In the STATE_TRANSFER_IN block, the condition to transition to STATE_TRANSFER_OUT is `((cycle_count_reg == CYCLE_COUNT-1) | input_axis_tlast)`. This allows a transition to output even when input_axis_tvalid is 0, causing output_axis_tvalid to assert (cycle 9 mismatch) and input_axis_tready to stay deasserted. The patch adds `&& (input_axis_tvalid)` so the transition only occurs when a valid input word is actually present, preserving backpressure semantics."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_31ff37e82a23",
      "failure_port": "output_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 267,
      "mechanism": "In the EXPAND_BUS branch of STATE_TRANSFER_OUT, the code enters the block when EXPAND_BUS is true and asserts output_axis_tvalid_int=1 unconditionally. When output_axis_tready_int is low, the FSM stays in STATE_TRANSFER_OUT and re-asserts output_axis_tvalid_int every cycle. The patch changes the entry guard from `EXPAND_BUS` to `(EXPAND_BUS) && (!output_axis_tready_int)`, preventing re-entry when the output side is not ready and thus stopping the spurious output_axis_tvalid=1 at cycle 9."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_2809cde8141f",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 203,
      "mechanism": "In the non-EXPAND_BUS branch of STATE_IDLE, input_axis_tready_next is set to 0 after the first word is accepted. The condition to move to STATE_TRANSFER_OUT is `if (input_axis_tvalid)`, which does not account for tlast. If tlast arrives without tvalid, the FSM can stall with input_axis_tready=0. The patch qualifies the tlast check with `&& (!input_axis_tlast)` so that a lone tlast does not block readiness, helping input_axis_tready recover to 1 at cycle 8."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_4366b56c71e4",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 250,
      "mechanism": "The STATE_TRANSFER_IN exit condition `((cycle_count_reg == CYCLE_COUNT-1) | input_axis_tlast)` can trigger when output_axis_tready_int is low, causing the FSM to move to STATE_TRANSFER_OUT while the output side is not ready. The patch adds `&& (!output_axis_tready_int)` so the FSM only exits when the output can actually accept data, keeping input_axis_tready asserted until the output pipeline clears."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_759e593ce41e",
      "failure_port": "output_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 250,
      "mechanism": "In STATE_TRANSFER_IN, the exit condition uses `input_axis_tlast` directly, which is a current-cycle input. When input_axis_tvalid=0 but tlast=1, the FSM transitions to STATE_TRANSFER_OUT and asserts output_axis_tvalid_int=1 based on stale temp registers. The patch adds `&& (!input_axis_tvalid)` so the transition only happens when a valid word accompanies tlast, eliminating the cycle 9 output_axis_tvalid=1 spike."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_86feac8aac1d",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 167,
      "mechanism": "In the EXPAND_BUS branch of STATE_IDLE, the first-word acceptance is guarded only by `EXPAND_BUS`. If tlast arrives without tvalid, the FSM can enter STATE_TRANSFER_OUT with invalid data. The patch changes the guard to `(EXPAND_BUS) && (input_axis_tlast)`, ensuring the first word is only accepted when tlast is asserted, which aligns readiness with frame boundaries and helps input_axis_tready reach 1 at cycle 8."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_6b110907b92c",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 203,
      "mechanism": "In the non-EXPAND_BUS branch of STATE_IDLE, the transition to STATE_TRANSFER_OUT only checks `input_axis_tvalid`. When output_axis_tready_int is low, the accepted word cannot be forwarded, but input_axis_tready is already lowered. The patch adds `&& (output_axis_tready_int)` so the FSM only commits to the transfer when the output side is ready, preventing premature deassertion of input_axis_tready at cycle 8."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_e805e9a3d4c9",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 240,
      "mechanism": "In the EXPAND_BUS branch of STATE_IDLE, the first-word capture is gated by `input_axis_tvalid`. If the first word has tlast but the output is not ready, the FSM enters STATE_TRANSFER_OUT and drops input_axis_tready. The patch adds `&& (!input_axis_tlast)` so that a single-cycle frame does not immediately transition out, giving the output pipeline time to assert ready and allowing input_axis_tready to stay high through cycle 8."
    }
  ],
  "explanation": "The three mismatches form a causal chain: cycle 8 input_axis_tready=0 (expected 1) -> FSM enters STATE_TRANSFER_OUT with output not ready -> cycle 9 output_axis_tvalid=1 (expected 0) and output_axis_tlast=0 (expected 1). The top patches directly address the state-machine guards that allow transitions when either input_axis_tvalid=0 or output_axis_tready_int=0. patch_c67689a4876b and patch_759e593ce41e fix the STATE_TRANSFER_IN exit condition by requiring input_axis_tvalid. patch_31ff37e82a23 fixes the STATE_TRANSFER_OUT re-entry guard in EXPAND_BUS mode. patch_4366b56c71e4 adds output_axis_tready_int awareness to the same exit. The remaining patches qualify entry guards in STATE_IDLE (patch_2809cde8141f, patch_86feac8aac1d, patch_6b110907b92c, patch_e805e9a3d4c9) to prevent premature commitment when tlast/tvalid/ready alignment is missing."
}
